From: TicWatch Pro 5 port
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: dwc3-msm: force vbus_active in peripheral mode

The T5 DT declares extcon=<charger eud>; without a charger vbus_active stays
false and the glue does not arm the cable (B_SESS_VLD) -> no pullup -> the host
does not enumerate even though the UDC exists. In dr_mode=peripheral we force it
(device-only).
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]
---

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c	2026-09-08 20:10:18.297637715 +0200
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c	2026-09-08 20:10:30.978234438 +0200
@@ -6002,6 +6002,19 @@
 		dwc3_ext_event_notify(mdwc);
 
 	dace_glue_step = 7;
+
+	/* dace: force vbus in peripheral mode. The T5 DT declares
+	 * extcon=<charger eud>, so the `!extcon` block above does not run and
+	 * vbus_active stays false -> the glue does not arm the cable
+	 * (B_SESS_VLD) -> no pullup -> the host never enumerates even though
+	 * the UDC exists and f_fs reads descriptors. Without the charger (the
+	 * real vbus source), we force it in device mode. */
+	if (mdwc->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL) {
+		mdwc->vbus_active = true;
+		dwc3_ext_event_notify(mdwc);
+		dev_info(mdwc->dev, "dace: vbus forced in peripheral\n");
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 
 put_dwc3:
